Usage: agent-deck session <command> [options]

Manage individual sessions.

Commands:
  start <id>              Start a session's tmux process
  stop <id>               Stop/kill session process
  remove <id>             Remove session from registry (stopped/error only; --force to bypass)
  cleanup [--days N]      Purge dead sessions idle N+ days (dry-run unless --yes)
  archive <id|title>      Stop session and hide it from active lists (retained in storage)
  unarchive <id|title>    Restore an archived session (does not restart it)
  restart [id] [--all] [--env KEY=VALUE]  Restart session (Claude: reload MCPs)
  revive [--all|--name]   Rebuild dead control pipes for errored sessions
  fork <id>               Fork Claude, OpenCode, Pi, Codex, or Oh My Pi session with context
  handoff <id>            Build a cross-tool handoff prompt from the session's conversation (read-only)
  switch-preview <id>     Preview switch capability, fidelity and refusals (read-only, no mutation)
  attach <id>             Attach to session interactively
  focus <id> [--attach]   Signal the running TUI to select (or --attach) a session
  recent [--limit N]      List sessions most-recently-used first (same last_accessed the TUI's alternate/MRU keys use)
  show [id]               Show session details (auto-detect current if no id)
  viewers [id]            List the terminals attached to a session (who is viewing it)
  current                 Show current session and profile (auto-detect)
  primer [id]             Show the resolved context-level and rendered primer/identity text (#2260; auto-detect current if no id)
  set <id> <field> <value>  Update session property
  switch <id> --to-harness <harness> [--to-account <account>]  Switch account or create a confirmed fresh cross-harness target
  switch-account <id> <account>  Switch Claude account and migrate the conversation
  move <id> <path>        Move session to a new path (migrates Claude history)
  send <id> <message>     Send a message to a running session (--queue: never silently lost, see send-status; --image <path>)
  send-status <send-id>   State of a queued send: queued, typed, submitted, landed or failed
  approve <id> [choice]   Resolve a visible Codex approval prompt
  output <id>             Get the last response from a session
  context [id]            Show what is loaded into the agent's context, ranked by cost
  children [id]           List sub-sessions with status + last completion
  ownership <cmd> <id>    Inspect/reconcile the processes a session owns (#1873)
  window close <id> <window> --yes  Kill one tmux window in a session (CLI parity for the TUI's window-row 'd')
  search <query>          Search message content across Claude sessions
  metrics <id>|--all      Per-session eval numbers from the local event journal (--json, --since)
  annotate <id>|--self    Record durable hints/tags (purpose, ticket, why, decision, outcome) for recall
  set-parent <id> <parent>  Link session as sub-session of parent
  unset-parent <id>       Remove sub-session link
  update <id> --no-parent          Alias for unset-parent <id>
  update <id> --parent <pid>       Alias for set-parent <id> <pid>
  set-transition-notify <id> <on|off>  Enable/disable transition notifications
  set-title-lock <id> <on|off>         Lock/unlock title from Claude session-name sync (#697)

Global Options:
  -p, --profile <name>   Use specific profile
  --json                 Output as JSON
  -q, --quiet            Minimal output (exit codes only)

Examples:
  agent-deck session start my-project
  agent-deck session stop abc123
  agent-deck session restart my-project
  agent-deck session restart --all                # Restart all active sessions
  agent-deck session fork my-project -t "my-project-fork"
  agent-deck session attach my-project
  agent-deck session show                  # Auto-detect current session
  agent-deck session show my-project --json
  agent-deck session set-parent sub-task main-project  # Make sub-task a sub-session
  agent-deck session unset-parent sub-task             # Remove sub-session link
  agent-deck session set-transition-notify worker off    # Suppress notifications
  agent-deck session set-transition-notify worker on     # Re-enable notifications
  agent-deck session set-title-lock SCRUM-351 on         # Prevent Claude from renaming it
  agent-deck session set-title-lock SCRUM-351 off        # Re-enable title sync
  agent-deck session output my-project                 # Get last response from session
  agent-deck session output my-project --json          # Get response as JSON
  agent-deck session context my-project                # What is in the agent's context
  agent-deck session context my-project --tab breakdown # Ranked by token cost
  agent-deck session context my-project --json         # Full report with provenance
  agent-deck session archive my-project                # Stop and hide the session
  agent-deck session unarchive my-project              # Restore an archived session
  agent-deck session recent                            # Most-recently-used sessions first
  agent-deck session recent --json --limit 5           # Same, machine-readable, top 5
  agent-deck session annotate auth-fix --ticket SB-412 --tag auth  # Durable hints for recall
  agent-deck session annotate --self --outcome worked  # An agent annotating its own session

Set command fields:
  title              Session title
  path               Project path
  command            Command to run
  tool               Tool type (claude, gemini, shell, etc.)
  wrapper            Wrapper command (use {command} to include tool command)
  claude-session-id  Claude conversation ID (for fork/resume)
  favorite           Favourite flag: true or false (favorite in list/show --json)
  gemini-session-id  Gemini conversation ID (for resume)
  tool-session-id    Custom [tools.*] conversation ID (resume_flag after reboot)

Set examples:
  agent-deck session set my-project title "New Title"
  agent-deck session set my-project claude-session-id "abc123-def456"
  agent-deck session set my-project tool-session-id "019f683f-..."
  agent-deck session set my-project tool claude
  agent-deck session set my-project wrapper "nvim +'terminal {command}'"
